pike Train Analysis & Neural Decoding

This project analyzes single-neuron spike trains recorded during an eye-movement direction tuning task. 
The work combines data analysis of peri-stimulus time histograms (PSTHs) and tuning curves with data science methods for decoding stimulus direction from neural activity.

📂 Project Structure

/data/ – Contains .mat files with single-neuron recordings. Each file is a MATLAB structure with:

spikes: T x N sparse matrix of spike trains (T = time in ms, N = trials).

target_direction: stimulus motion direction in degrees (0–315°).

target_motion: motion onset and offset times (ms).

my_classifier.m – Custom classifier function to decode stimulus direction from test spike trains.

test_classifier.m – Provided function to evaluate classifiers with k-leave-out cross-validation.

run_test.m – Script to benchmark classifiers across multiple neurons.

plots/ – Raster plots, PSTHs, tuning curves, and model fits.

📊 Analysis Steps

Raster Plots

Visualize spike trains per trial, separated by target direction.

Implemented using MATLAB’s spy function.

PSTHs (Peri-Stimulus Time Histograms)

Compute firing rate in 1 ms bins.

Smooth with a 30 ms square window.

Normalize to spikes/second.

Display all 8 directions in a single plot.

Direction Tuning Curves

Compute average firing rate during motion per direction.

Fit with:

Cosine function

Von-Mises function

Von-Mises + baseline term

Compare fits using goodness of fit metrics (e.g., R², mean squared error, AIC/BIC).

Estimate the neuron’s preferred direction from fits and directly from data.

Classifier

Function my_classifier(train_data, test_spikes) predicts stimulus direction from spike trains.

Evaluated with cross-validation via test_classifier.m.

Metrics:

success_id: fraction of correctly predicted directions.

success_angle: mean angular error (degrees).

⚖️ Key Questions Addressed

How does a neuron’s firing rate depend on stimulus direction?

Which tuning model (cosine, von-Mises, von-Mises+baseline) fits best?

How to quantify goodness of fit and trade-offs with model complexity?

Can we decode stimulus direction from spike trains using statistical classifiers?

🧰 Tools & Libraries

MATLAB (core analysis, plotting, fitting)

Functions: spy, smooth, fittype, fit, cosd

🚀 Results Overview

PSTHs reveal direction-selective firing increases during motion.

Tuning curves show clear orientation preference, best fit by a von-Mises distribution.

Classifier achieves significantly better accuracy than random baseline (success_id ≫ 0.12, success_angle ≪ 90°).

Differences observed across neurons in preferred direction and tuning sharpness.

📌 Learning Outcomes

Hands-on experience with neural data analysis and decoding methods.

Comparison of model fits and interpretation of tuning curves.

Implementation of a supervised classifier for spike-train data.

Understanding trade-offs between descriptive analysis and predictive modeling.
